'''Jatiel''' (from [[W:Arabic language|Bayani]] جاتيل, meaning "sandy waterside [village]"), also spelled '''Satiel''', is a [[w:Port|port city]] in the region of [[Luzamontaña]] within the [[Communities of Balisca|community]] of [[Araucaria]]. Jatiel is located within the [[Concordia|Concordia conurbation]] and lies on the southwest of the [[Tiburón headlands]], where the [[Guadalquivir]] empties into the [[Aethiopian Ocean]]. It is the principle port for the [[Castejón Metropolis]] and the wider conurbation. Additionally, Jatiel is home to [[Jaraco Aerospace Base]], a major facility of the [[Confederal Aerospace Force|Aerospace Force]]. It is the second largest city in Araucaria after [[Axarquía]].

Founded in September 1622 by self-liberated slaves and convicts, it gradually grew into one of the largest [[W:Quilombo|quilombo]]<nowiki/>s in the Americas and became a haven for freedman and indigenous people fleeing colonial rule during the [[Maroon Wars]]. Despite opposition from mining prospectors and the representatives of the republic of [[Hesperia]], Jatiel and the surrounding territory were definitively recognized as part of the [[Maroon Confederacy]] in 1838. Following the devastation brought to [[Axarquía]] by [[1853 Gran Sur earthquake|Gran Sur earthquake]], the city served as the [[W:Temporary capital|interim capital]] of the [[Maroon Confederacy]]. The city became economically tied to the [[Northern Confederation]] earlier than the rest of the Maroon Confederacy due to it's proximity to the [[Alpujarra]], and following [[1883 Confederal Convention|Araucaria's confederation]] it rapidly grew into a major shipping port in eastern [[Abyala]]. Beginning in the 20th century and continuing through the beginning of the 21st, the city has regained economic dynamism with the expansion of the [[Jatiel Metro]], the expansion of commuter rail networks, open development policies, improved security and improved education.

The city is promoted domestically and internationally as a leisure destination and is considered a global city type "Beta +" by the [[Adonia Globalization and World Cities Ranks|Globalization and World Cities Network]]. It is known for its mild year-round [[W:Mediterranean climate|Mediterranean climate]], extensive [[W:List of beaches in San Diego County|beaches]] and [[List of parks in Jatiel|parks]], long association with the [[Confederal Aerospace Force|Aerospace Force]], and recent emergence as a healthcare and [[W:Biotechnology|biotechnology]] development center.   

