==Environment and geography==

===Climate===
Jatiel has a warm-summer [[W:Mediterranean climate|Mediterranean climate]] influenced on the coast by the [[W:Benguela Current|Benguela Current]]. As in any Mediterranean climate, the city experiences a dry, warm summer but temperatures rarely exceed {{convert|30|°C|F|abbr=on|lk=out}} due to the influence of the maritime current offshore. Summer nights are cool with temperatures around {{convert|16|°C|F|abbr=on|lk=out}}. Winters are damp and cool with daily high temperatures ranging from {{convert|13|to|17|C|F|abbr=on}} and from {{convert|5|to|9|C|F|abbr=on}} at night, rarely falling below freezing. Spring and autumn can vary from mild to cool. The rain falls mainly in autumn and winter, with July being the rainiest (107&nbsp;mm). The average annual rainfall totals 480&nbsp;mm.
