==Culture and society==
{{Main|Culture of Jatiel}}
The culture of Jatiel is influenced heavily by the mixing of [[Culture of Balisca|Baliscan culture]] with diverse international influences, due to the city's position on the [[Levante, Balisca|Baliscan Levante]], its large [[Immigration to Balisca|immigrant]] population, and its history as part of the [[Maroon Confederacy]] on the frontier of the emergent [[Northern Confederation]]. Jatiel's longtime association with the [[Confederal Armed Forces|Baliscan military]] also contributes to its culture.

=== Cuisine ===
{{See also|Cuisine of Balisca}}
Because of its ethnic and cultural mix, Jatiel has a wide range of cuisines. One can find Nusarayan, Monsoran, Volisanian, Sartan, "THAI", Dagiti, "VIETNAMESE", Aetolian, Abyalan, Breislandic, Kemali, Central and East Fosian, Levantine and Oceanic food throughout the city. In addition, there are numerous seafood restaurants and steakhouses. 

Jatiel's warm, dry climate and access to the ocean have also made it a center for fishing and for growing fruits and vegetables. Long a center of the tuna industry, Jatiel benefits from an abundant supply of seafood.

Many of the most popular restaurants can be found in the Azafor barrio, [[Asikyira]], Córdoba, Guaraci, and Ciudad Roja.

Local specialties include:
[[File:Pollo asado fries.png|thumb|Pollo asado fries]]

* Araucarian (empanadas, street tacos, fish tacos, choripán, [[W:Pollo asado|pollo asada fries]], and ceviche)
* Kemali ([[W:Butter Chicken|Butter chicken]], chicken tikka masala, naan, tandoori, [[W:Biryani|Biryani]])
* North Fosian specialties of all kinds
* Seafood of all kinds
* Local [[W:Wine|wines]]
* Various fruits and vegetables (including avocados, tomatoes, mushrooms, olives, eggplant, oranges, lemons, limes, strawberries, grapefruit, grapes, apples, pomegranates, persimmons, and melons)

